    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "==Here is the latest inventory data for this sync cycle, pulled from all three sources.\n\nSHOPIFY (Admin API - inventory_levels):\n{{ JSON.stringify($('Shopify HTTP Node').all().map(i => i.json)) }}\n\nAMAZON (SP-API - catalog/inventory):\n{{ JSON.stringify($('Amazon HTTP Node').all().map(i => i.json)) }}\n\nPHYSICAL COUNTER (Google Sheet, manually updated by staff):\n{{ JSON.stringify($('Get row(s) in sheet').all().map(i => i.json)) }}\n\nCompare these three sources per product/SKU. Update the connected Google Sheets tool with the correct current quantity and status for each product, and flag anything that looks like a race condition — a sale reflected on one platform but not yet on another.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "I run a small home decor brand (UrbanCraft Home) — candles, diffusers, that kind of stuff. We sell on our Shopify store, Amazon, and also have a small physical counter at a local market where my sister manages sales manually in a register.\n\nProblem: during our Diwali sale last year we oversold two of our bestsellers — someone bought online right after we'd already sold the last piece offline, and we had to refund + apologize. Been manually checking stock across all three every morning since, it's a mess.\n\nYou will be given the purchase details every 5mins so that you can make a google sheet out of the data which I can see and know about the status of the products.\n I will attach a google sheets tool too, in which you can see the quantities of products remaining along with other basic details of the product and I want you update that data based on the orders placed.\nAfter comparing sources once, call the update tool immediately — do not re-read the sheet more than once per cycle.\n\nIn output I don't want any text, not a single word, the only acceptable output is the name of the platform on which the order was placed,\n\"platform\" : \"amazon\" | \"shopify\"",
          "maxIterations": 10
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        704,
        -32
      ],
      "id": "c1c6751a-9f6d-47a9-8e69-255c620e98f0",
